    "done_when": "Make every production pick record where its time went, so a pick that hits the 5 s bound can be attributed. Today a timed-out pick records only fallback_reason timeout. For example, runs r-20261007T180232994727-a-stopped-host-names-its-reason and r-20261007T180051854323-review-of-picker-helpers-have-one-owner timed out after the one-pass fix landed, while two other picks finished in about 650 ms. The pick-latency census (~/.config/reckon/crew/reports/reckon/pick-latency-census/report.md) measured the stages offline only.\n\n1. In reckon/crew/picker/__init__.py, pick() times each stage it runs: the candidates snapshot, the estimated-context figure, prompt rendering (state and questions), and the Jev request (connect plus response). It appends one JSON line per pick to a pick-timings log under the crew home. Each line carries the request's node id, session and a start timestamp, each stage's milliseconds, the outcome, and whether the pick finished within the bound. Resolve the log path the way the crew home's other logs resolve, so a test's RECKON_HOME isolation covers it.\n2. A pick that finishes after dispatch has given up still writes its line when it completes. The daemon thread keeps running, so its stages stay attributable.\n3. A failure to write the log never fails or slows the pick. Use a bounded, best-effort append.\n4. Tests in tests/test_pick_records_its_stage_times.py:\n   - a pick with a stub Jev client writes one line with every stage present;\n   - a deliberately slow stub stage beyond the bound still produces a line once it completes, marked as past the bound;\n   - an unwritable log path leaves the pick's result unchanged;\n   - the real crew home is untouched under RECKON_HOME isolation.\n\nDo not edit reckon/crew/dispatch.py or reckon/cli.py; they are on hold for a module split. Do not edit reckon/crew/picker/lane_context.py, snapshot.py, types.py, prompts.py or templates/; a lane-and-model run owns them next. Gate: tests/test_pick_records_its_stage_times.py, every tests/test_picker*.py, tests/test_pick_candidates_one_pass.py and tests/test_jev_weighs_context.py. Run with the main checkout's .venv/bin/python -m pytest -p no:cacheprovider -n 8 in the FOREGROUND, with one log each for base and head under the run directory, each ending in an EXIT line, judged by delta. Write the evidence fragment docs/evidence/fragments/one-typesafe-model-picker/pick-records-its-stage-times.html.",
    "estimated_hours": 1.5,
    "goal": "Every production pick records its per-stage times, including a pick that finishes after the bound",
